---
import Layout from '~/layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from 'astrowind:config';

const crumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', href: '/' },
  { name: 'R&D Center', href: '/randdcenter' },
  { name: 'Hull Engineering Studio' },
];

const metadata = {
  title: `Hull Engineering Studio — CAD, FEA & Custom Hull Design | ${SITE.name}`,
  description: `Explore our Hull Engineering Studio for CAD design, finite element analysis (FEA), and custom high-performance SUP hull development. Contact our engineering team to start your next board project.`,
};
---

<Layout metadata={metadata} breadcrumbs={crumbs}>
  <section class="px-6 sm:px-6 py-16 sm:py-20 mx-auto max-w-5xl">
    <a href="/randdcenter" class="text-sm text-gray-500 hover:underline">&larr; Back to R&D Center</a>
    <div class="mt-4 grid md:grid-cols-5 gap-10">
      <div class="md:col-span-3">
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-primary uppercase tracking-wider">Lab 02</p>
        <h1 class="mt-2 text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold">Hull Engineering Studio</h1>
        <p class="mt-3 text-lg text-muted">Digital simulation, structural intelligence, custom hull design</p>
      </div>
      <div class="md:col-span-2">
        <img
          src="https://assets.afarer.com/images/afarer/factory/design discussafarer-inflatable-boat-afarer-factory-exterior.webp"
          alt="afarer hull engineering CAD design workstation"
          class="w-full h-48 object-cover rounded-xl"
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="px-6 sm:px-6 pb-12 mx-auto max-w-4xl prose prose-gray dark:prose-invert">
    <h2>Where strength meets hydrodynamics</h2>
    <p>
      The hull is the backbone of any inflatable SUP. It must be light enough to glide efficiently, strong enough to
      handle rocky shorelines, and rigid enough to convert every paddle stroke into forward motion. At {SITE.name}, our
      Hull Engineering Studio combines advanced CAD modelling, finite element analysis (FEA), and decades of practical
      board-design experience to deliver hulls that are optimised for their intended discipline — not generic shapes
      adapted from a catalogue.
    </p>
    <p>
      We work with three primary construction platforms — reinforced drop-stitch PVC cores, hand-laid fibreglass
      laminates, and rotationally moulded polyethylene — and have the engineering capability to design, simulate, and
      validate each one in-house.
    </p>

    <h2>Design tools and standards</h2>
    <p>Our digital engineering environment includes:</p>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Capability</th><th>Software / Tool</th><th>Application</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr
          ><td>3D parametric modelling</td><td>SolidWorks Professional</td><td
            >Hull surface, rail and stringer reinforcement, deck layout, gear-mount points</td
          ></tr
        >
        <tr
          ><td>Finite element analysis</td><td>ANSYS Mechanical &amp; LS-DYNA</td><td
            >Stress mapping, modal analysis, crash/impact simulation</td
          ></tr
        >
        <tr
          ><td>Computational fluid dynamics</td><td>Ansys Fluent / Star-CCM+</td><td
            >Hydrodynamic drag prediction, trim optimisation</td
          ></tr
        >
        <tr
          ><td>Laminate engineering</td><td>ESAComp / CADEC</td><td
            >Fibreglass layer stacking, core selection, weight estimation</td
          ></tr
        >
        <tr><td>Mould flow simulation</td><td>Moldex3D</td><td>Rotomoulding wall-thickness prediction</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2>Our engineering workflow</h2>
    <p>
      Every hull design, whether it is a standard model or a fully custom project, follows a rigorous five-stage
      process:
    </p>
    <ol>
      <li>
        <strong>Concept &amp; requirements gathering</strong> — We meet with you to define rider weight and payload, speed
        envelope, water-state capability, transport requirements, and any special mission equipment (deck mounts, cargo
        tie-down positions, accessory integration).
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>3D surfacing &amp; hydrostatic calculation</strong> — The hull form is modelled in SolidWorks and checked for
        hydrostatic stability, volume distribution, and righting moment using built-in analysis tools.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Structural FEA</strong> — Load cases are defined: static (rider + gear), dynamic (wave-landing impacts at 5g),
        and grounding (striking a rocky shoreline at 3 m/s). Stress contours are reviewed; safety factor &ge; 2.5 is mandatory.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>CFD drag optimisation</strong> — The hull is simulated at three loading conditions and five speeds. Wetted
        surface area, trim angle, and residual resistance are iteratively reduced.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Design review &amp; release</strong> — The complete engineering package (3D model, FEA report, CFD report,
        weight estimate, ply book) is reviewed by our senior engineer before release to the prototype workshop.
      </li>
    </ol>

    <div class="not-prose my-10 p-6 rounded-xl bg-gray-50 dark:bg-gray-900 border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-800">
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-gray-500 mb-3 uppercase tracking-wider">
        FEA Stress Distribution — Touring SUP Hull (Reinforced Drop-Stitch)
      </p>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-4 text-sm">
        <div class="p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 bg-white dark:bg-gray-950">
          <span class="block text-2xl font-bold text-blue-600">2.8 : 1</span>
          <span class="text-gray-500">Safety factor at max payload</span>
        </div>
        <div class="p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 bg-white dark:bg-gray-950">
          <span class="block text-2xl font-bold text-blue-600">15.2 %</span>
          <span class="text-gray-500">Drag reduction vs previous generation</span>
        </div>
        <div class="p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 bg-white dark:bg-gray-950">
          <span class="block text-2xl font-bold text-blue-600">87 kN/m&sup2;</span>
          <span class="text-gray-500">Peak slamming pressure (design limit)</span>
        </div>
        <div class="p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 bg-white dark:bg-gray-950">
          <span class="block text-2xl font-bold text-blue-600">18 000 h</span>
          <span class="text-gray-500">Cumulative FEA runtime in 2025</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2>Customisation: your hull, your rules</h2>
    <p>
      No two paddlers have identical requirements. A fishing SUP needs a wide, stable planing hull; a touring board
      needs a displacement hull that maximises glide; a surf SUP needs responsive rails and tuned rocker. We do not
      force your application into a pre-existing hull shape. We design from your specification upward.
    </p>
    <p>Examples of recent custom hull engineering projects:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>A stretched-length touring SUP for a Caribbean eco-tour operator, with a reinforced bow for beach landings.</li>
      <li>A high-visibility patrol SUP for a harbour authority, with integrated gear mounts and tactical rails.</li>
      <li>An expedition touring SUP for a rental fleet, with reinforced rails and extra cargo tie-downs.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Our engineers</h2>
    <p>
      The studio is led by a senior engineer with 14 years of experience in high-performance board design, supported by
      two mechanical engineers specialised in FEA and CFD. All three hold advanced degrees in marine or mechanical
      engineering from internationally recognised universities. The team publishes regularly in industry journals
      and presents at international conferences on high-performance paddle-sport engineering.
    </p>

    <h2>Partner with us on your next hull</h2>
    <p>
      From the first concept sketch to the final stress report, our Hull Engineering Studio is your partner in creating
      a board that is not just built — but engineered. We invest the simulation hours upfront so that every weld, every
      laminate layer, and every curve of the hull is there for a reason.
    </p>
    <p>
      Whether you need a minor modification to an existing model or a completely clean-sheet design, we are ready to
      discuss your requirements.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="px-6 sm:px-6 pb-20 mx-auto max-w-4xl text-center">
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-800 bg-gray-50 dark:bg-gray-900 p-8">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">Start your hull design consultation</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted">Tell us about your mission profile and we will propose an engineering path.</p>
      <a
        href="/contact"
        class="mt-4 inline-block px-6 py-3 bg-primary text-white font-semibold rounded-md hover:bg-primary/90"
        >Contact our engineering team</a
      >
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
